CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a009144-7fb64372-017f-f2fa77e0-000007ea:Runton\, R
 ajashi
CREATED:20260609T170539Z
DESCRIPTION:Human health changes continuously through movement\, speech\, 
 sleep\, behavior\, and environment\, yet most medical AI still relies on 
 episodic clinical measurements and retrospective records\, missing how di
 sease risk and functional decline emerge in everyday life. In this talk\,
  I will show how this agenda spans a continuum from what people do\, to w
 hat happens inside the body\, to how they feel\, and ultimately to how in
 telligent systems can support them. Through wireless sensing\, mobile and
  wearable computing\, biochemical sensing\, and edge AI\, my work develop
 s low-burden systems that recover latent behavioral\, physiological\, and
  affective states from weak real-world signals\, including WiFi-based fal
 l detection\, fine-grained hand motion reconstruction\, continuous lipid 
 profiling\, pain biomarkers\, and proactive mental health support. The br
 oader goal is to build cyber-physical intelligence that helps shift healt
 hcare from late clinical reaction to everyday prevention and intervention
 .
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260609T170539Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260630T100000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260609T170539Z
